<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  M3 table for the command line: riley-agent called as Claude Code, as Pi (and, as extras, as Codex and from a
  plain shell), against a private riley-agentd in a sandbox with a fake Hyprland. Read by tests/cli/gate.py.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

  Every expected result was worked out by hand from the plan and tests/policy/cases.xml (the M1 table) before the
  command line was changed for M3. Expected results are never changed to make a test pass. Disputes go to the lead.

  ============================================================================================
  THE SANDBOX (what is true for every call; see tests/run-cli.sh)
    - No /dev/uinput, no Wayland or X socket, no session bus, no real Hyprland socket: an allowed action fails
      harmlessly after its decision (no mouse, no grim picture, no AT-SPI tree, Hyprland dispatch answers an error,
      launch finds no such program). So "allow" is seen as: first line "failed ...", exit 4, and the service log's
      line for the request says decision="allow" reason="allowed" rule="<permission id>" result="failed".
    - The fake Hyprland serves the one <desk> below: j/monitors, j/clients, j/activewindow (the call's "active"
      window, or {} when none), j/cursorpos; every /dispatch is answered with an error.
    - A window's "process" (claude, pi or codex) is a process of that name the gate starts in the sandbox; the
      service finds it as the window's process (rule R6c, agent terminal). Other windows have pid 0.
    - Callers: claude, pi, codex = riley-agent run as the child of a copy of a small launcher binary of that name
      (the service sees comm claude / pi / codex among the caller's ancestors: client claude-code / pi / codex).
      shell = riley-agent run from bash with no coding agent among its ancestors (the sandbox's own process
      namespace hides the agent the gate itself runs under): the service identifies no client ("").
    - PASSWORD FIELDS: there is no accessibility bus. The service asks AT-SPI only for type and key into the focused
      window (R9), and then cannot tell: the sandbox fact is password=unknown. When the target is not focused the
      service does not ask, and the fact is password=false.
    - FOCUS MOVED cannot be planted (it needs a password=false focused field first). Cases with focus-moved are
      derived (below).
  CALL ATTRIBUTES
    id         this table's id (k...)
    m1         the M1 case it maps (tests/policy/cases.xml), when any
    kind       m1      the M1 case's facts as the sandbox can show them; the expected result is the M1 case's own.
                       The gate checks the facts and the expected result against the M1 table itself. A fact may
                       differ from M1 only when M1's deciding rule comes before the rule that reads that fact
                       (password: R9; focused, focus-moved: R11; both only for type and key): it cannot change
                       the result. The <why> says which rule decides.
               derived the M1 case with a fact the sandbox cannot show (password true or false into a focused field,
                       focus moved); <differs> names it, and the expected result is worked out by hand for the
                       sandbox's facts with the M1 rules.
               extra   no M1 case: a call needed for coverage or for checks 2, 3, 6; worked out by hand.
    check      which gate check it belongs to (1 to 9, see tests/run-cli.sh)
    caller     claude | pi | codex | shell
    command    the riley-agent subcommand
    window     a <desk> window id, passed as the window option with its ADDRESS (see writes to a 0700 folder under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR)
    active     the <desk> window that has focus during the call (absent: none)
    text / <text><part>: TEXT for type, joined at run time (token-shaped test strings never appear whole; all fake)
    key, app   NAME for key, APP for launch. point and click use X Y = 10 10 (inside every desk window).
    expect     allow    see above
               refused  first line "refused <reason>", exit 1; log line decision="deny" reason=<reason>
                        result="refused" (and rule=<rule> when given); for resume a control line result="refused"
               list     windows: first line "ok N windows", exit 0, N listing lines; <item> windows listed or not;
                        log line decision="allow" rule="per-window" result="done"
               ok       stop, segfault, resume: first line "ok ...", exit 0; log control line result="done"
               help     check 4
    targets    the planted fault this call must catch
  STEPS between calls: <restart/> kills the service by PID (SIGKILL), removes the bar state file, and starts it again
    with the same home and state folder; <bar state="..."/> reads $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/riley-desktop-agent/state.json.
    Check 7 (lead addendum, stop-state hardening) adds:
    <restart wipe="true"/>    as <restart/>, and before the start it also deletes the persisted stop copy
                              ($XDG_STATE_HOME/riley-desktop-agent/stopped, docs/files.md) and the service's whole
                              runtime folder $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/riley-desktop-agent (state.json, the socket and anything
                              else the service keeps there): only log.xml and hash-secret are left. That is a reboot
                              (the runtime folder is gone) plus a deleted stop copy.
    <persisted present="true|false"/>  the persisted stop copy is there (then: a file, mode 0600, its folder 0700, as
                              docs/files.md "stopped" says) or not there.
    <startlog contains="stop"/>  the lines the service wrote to log.xml since the last restart (before any call):
                              at least one, each one XML element, and one of them has an attribute value containing
                              the word (the addendum: "the service starts STOPPED and logs why").
  THE SANDBOX EXAMPLE (check 8) and the docs (check 9) are in <sandbox-example> at the end; see there.
  ============================================================================================
-->
