  <!-- ================= check 7: the stop survives a lost stop copy (lead addendum, stop-state hardening) =================
       The rule worked out by hand from the addendum, before the code: at start, if the persisted stop copy is missing
       but the last control line in log.xml says stop or segfault with no later resume whose result is done, the
       service starts STOPPED (bar "stopped", every request refused "stopped" by R3) and logs why. A resume that R0
       refused (result="refused") is not a resume done: it leaves the stop in force, in the log as in the service.
       If the last stop or segfault is followed by a resume done, the service starts idle (R3 does not apply).
       Planted fault stop-log-check-removed compiles that start-up check out: after a wiped restart the service
       starts idle, so the bar reads "idle" and the requests are decided as if never stopped (allow p-cc-see,
       allow p-pi-all): the steps marked targets="stop-log-check-removed" fail. -->
