  <!-- ================= checks 8 and 9: the sandbox example and the docs (lead addendum) =================
       Run by tests/run-cli.sh in a second bwrap sandbox ("decoy host"), like the first, but where every path a
       coding agent could use to reach the desktop without riley-agent EXISTS as a harmless decoy:
         /dev/uinput                          bound to /dev/null (writes go nowhere)
         $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wayland-0           a socket the gate binds and never serves; WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0
         /tmp/.X11-unix/X0                    the same for X; DISPLAY=:0
         $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hypr/<signature>/   the gate's fake Hyprland (it never dispatches)
       A private riley-agentd runs with the config below, at its default paths in the home below. The wrapper
       tools/riley-sandbox is called as documented in docs/agents.md:
           cd <project> && tools/riley-sandbox COMMAND [ARGS...]
       (the project = the current folder, bound read-write; $HOME bound; the riley-agent socket
       $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/riley-desktop-agent/agentd.sock bound at the same path; no /dev/uinput, no Wayland or X
       socket, no $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hypr; WAYLAND_DISPLAY and DISPLAY unset). COMMAND is tests/cli/sandbox-probe.sh,
       copied into the project folder, run as Claude Code (the wrapper is the child of the launcher copy named
       claude). The same probe is also run WITHOUT the wrapper ("bare"), to show it sees every decoy: a probe that
       cannot see them would prove nothing.
       Expected values, by hand from the addendum ("no /dev/uinput, no WAYLAND_DISPLAY/DISPLAY sockets, no
       $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hypr, but WITH the riley-agent socket bound in", "$HOME and the project bound") and, for
       config and state, from the plan (deny-always: the tool's own config) and the addendum (deleting the stop state
       is one of the ways around riley-agent): a sandboxed agent must not be able to change config.xml or write in
       the service's state folder (where the stop copy and log.xml live). -->
